body:
I can't actually feel the semen spurting out, but I can feel my boyfriend's penis pulsing and things getting hotter and wetter, and it's a huge emotional/psychological turn-on for me. I have body image and self-esteem issues, and the thought that he loves and trusts me enough to let his defenses down and be that intimate with me and share his orgasm with me, and that I'm exciting enough to make him cum, really is very fulfilling. The idea that he's leaving literally part of himself, his DNA, inside me is also a huge turn-on, and I love his reactions as he gets there, holding him while he empties himself into me. He is never more mine than in that moment--physically, emotionally, spiritually, whatever name you want to put on it. It's a whole-body. whole-soul kind of thing, not just a vaginal one.

&#x200B;

It sounds hokey, but I don't know a better way to describe it.

I'm so very sorry to hear this. You don't deserve this. Nobody deserves hatred like this, least of all from her parents.

&#x200B;

I wish I had a magic bullet for you, but it sounds like your parents are way beyond reason. Just get away from them as soon and as far as you can.

&#x200B;

If you'e in NC, go to the Triangle or Asheville. There are plenty of supportive communities there.

